[
  {
    "id": "bl-bdj",
    "title": "Formula v2 step targets (gc.run-operator) fail to resolve from HQ scope: 'unknown formulas v2 target'",
    "description": "REPRO (bright-lights, gc 1.4.1): sling build-basic onto an HQ bead\n(e.g. bl-5zi) with an HQ-scoped target -\u003e\n\n  instantiating formula \"build-basic\" on bl-5zi: step build-basic.prepare:\n  unknown formulas v2 target \"gc.run-operator\"\n\nSame sling with a rig-scoped target (hello-world/gc.run-operator) works,\nbecause the default route then supplies the ambient rig context.\n\nROOT CAUSE (source: internal/graphroute + cmd/gc/cmd_agent.go):\n- Roles-pack agents resolve to config Agent{name: \"run-operator\", dir:\n  \"hello-world\", binding: \"gc\"} -\u003e QualifiedName \"hello-world/gc.run-operator\".\n- build-basic's step metadata gc.run_target = \"gc.run-operator\" (bare,\n  binding-qualified).\n- ResolveGraphStepBindingWithVars derives executionRigContext from the\n  default route (graphroute.go:519). For an HQ target there is no slash -\u003e\n  rigContext \"\" -\u003e ambient step skipped.\n- resolveAgentIdentity (cmd_agent.go:348) then tries: literal qualified\n  (no match), pool instances (no), bare scan `a.Name == input` (config\n  Name is \"run-operator\", never equals \"gc.run-operator\") -\u003e unknown.\n\nMINIMAL FIX: in the step-3 bare-name scans (cmd/gc/cmd_agent.go\nresolveAgentIdentity AND internal/agentutil/resolve.go ResolveAgent),\nalso accept the binding-qualified bare form:\n\n  if a.Name == input || a.BindingQualifiedName() == input {\n\nThis matches the documented identity form \"gastown.mayor\" (dot/binding-\nqualified bare name) and makes pack-prefixed role targets resolvable\nwhenever unambiguous.\n\nFOLLOW-UPS (design questions, not blocking):\n- Multi-rig cities (\u003e=2 rigs with the roles pack): a bare\n  \"gc.run-operator\" step target will become ambiguous (N matches) when\n  routed from HQ scope. Better error than today, but consider falling\n  back to the store-owning rig context (rootStoreRef ScopeRigContext,\n  already computed for controlRigContext) when the default route has no\n  rig context.\n- gascity.el transient could hint when a formula path is chosen from HQ\n  scope with rig-only targets.\n\nVerified: repro'd on scratch bead bl-ab8 (closed no-op) in\nbright-lights; dry-run alone does NOT exercise this path (routing plan\nonly) — instantiation does.",
    "status": "open",
    "priority": 1,
    "issue_type": "task",
    "owner": "roman@burningswell.com",
    "created_at": "2026-09-16T12:20:21Z",
    "created_by": "mayor",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-16T12:20:21Z",
